From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:19:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: keep the pending RADIUS messages of a non-AP MLD
 at a link STA free

The links of an AP MLD share the RADIUS client of the first BSS, and
the EAPOL state machine of a non-AP MLD sends its Access-Requests with
the MLD address. ap_free_sta() flushes the pending authentication
messages of sta->addr, which is the MLD address for every affiliated
STA. The free of a link STA, at an AP removal of a link that is not
the association link or of the old association STA after a move of the
association, drops the pending Access-Request of the MLD, which stays
associated. The Access-Accept or Access-Challenge then finds no
request, and the EAP authentication stalls.

Flush only at the free of the association STA.

Depends on 836-AP-MLD-keep-the-association-of-a-non-AP-MLD-at-a-lin.patch.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -591,7 +591,9 @@
 
 	rsn_preauth_free_station(hapd, sta);
 #ifndef CONFIG_NO_RADIUS
-	if (hapd->radius)
+	/* The links of an AP MLD share the RADIUS client, and the pending
+	 * messages of a non-AP MLD belong to its association STA. */
+	if (hapd->radius && !hostapd_sta_is_link_sta(hapd, sta))
 		radius_client_flush_auth(hapd->radius, sta->addr);
 #endif /* CONFIG_NO_RADIUS */
 
